From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:36:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset, nvidia-drm: run the vblank delivery threads
 at low RT priority

Vblank callbacks reach nvidia-drm through the NVKMS kthread queue: RM's
RG semaphore event schedules an NVKMS timer, the nvidia-modeset/kthread_q
thread runs it under the NVKMS lock and calls into nvidia-drm. Both that
thread and the nvidia-drm vblank worker, which enables the callback for the
first flip after an idle period, are normal tasks with nice 0. On a loaded
system they compete with everything else, and with a sched_ext scheduler
such as scx_lavd they are scheduled like any other task.

Compositors already run their commit path at RT priority: KWin, for
example, uses CAP_SYS_NICE to put its main thread and its per-output
threads at SCHED_RR 1. The thread that delivers the events those threads
wait for was the only link in that chain without RT priority.

When the callback comes more than 50 ms late, nvidia-drm sends the flip
event from its timeout with a timestamp that is not the flip's vblank; one
such event showed up during a parallel build with all cores busy. Without
that timeout, a late callback just delays the flip event and shows up as a
missed frame.

Run both threads at the lowest SCHED_FIFO priority with
sched_set_fifo_low(), the same level as such compositor threads. RT tasks
are not handled by sched_ext. Both threads only take locks shared with
process context (nvkms_lock, the DRM event lock), so waiting for them does
not change compared to now; they only get on a CPU sooner once they can
run. NVKMS polls hardware in some timer callbacks with nvkms_yield() and
short udelay() waits, which no longer lets normal tasks onto that CPU
meanwhile; the fair and sched_ext deadline servers still leave them their
share of each period.

Kernels before 5.9 have no sched_set_fifo_low() and keep the old
behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c           | 10 ++++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
index 13c79039..a3751afb 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
@@ -86,6 +86,8 @@
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include <linux/sort.h>
+#include <linux/sched.h>
+#include <linux/version.h>
 
 /*
  * Commit fcd70cd36b9b ("drm: Split out drm_probe_helper.h")
@@ -1138,6 +1140,14 @@ static int nv_drm_dev_load(struct drm_device *dev)
         if (!nv_drm_workthread_init(&nv_dev->vblank_worker, "nvidia-drm-vblank-notification")) {
             NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_WARN(nv_dev, "Failed to init vblank worker, vblank notification not enabled.");
         } else {
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 9, 0)
+            /*
+             * Enabling vblank callbacks for the first flip after an idle
+             * period goes through this worker; keep it from waiting behind
+             * normal tasks, like the NVKMS queue that delivers them.
+             */
+            sched_set_fifo_low(nv_dev->vblank_worker.q.q_kthread);
+#endif
 #if defined(NV_DRM_CRTC_FUNCS_HAS_GET_VBLANK_TIMESTAMP)
             /* See nv_drm_crtc_get_vblank_counter() */
             dev->max_vblank_count = NV_DRM_RASTER_FRAME_MASK;
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
index dcd085b3..3f33654d 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include <asm/div64.h> /* do_div() */
 #include <linux/sched.h>
 #include <linux/sched/signal.h>
+#include <linux/version.h>
 #include <linux/wait.h>
 #include <linux/random.h>
 #include <linux/file.h>
@@ -2241,6 +2242,19 @@ static int __init nvkms_init(void)
         goto fail_kthread;
     }
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 9, 0)
+    /*
+     * Vblank and flip completion callbacks reach nvidia-drm through this
+     * queue (RM event -> nvkms timer -> this thread). As a normal task it
+     * competes with everything else on a loaded system, and a callback
+     * that is late by more than a frame makes nvidia-drm send the flip
+     * event from its timeout with a stale timestamp. Run it at the lowest
+     * RT priority, like other kernel threads that sit in a latency path;
+     * this also keeps it out of sched_ext schedulers.
+     */
+    sched_set_fifo_low(nvkms_kthread_q.q_kthread);
+#endif
+
     ret = nv_kthread_q_init(&nvkms_deferred_close_kthread_q,
                             "nvidia-modeset/deferred_close_kthread_q");
     if (ret != 0) {
